champion " [:a {:href "/athletes/3455"} "Dick McTaggart"] " had a spectacular games and was awarded the Val Barker Trophy as the outstanding boxer of the Games."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The USA, traditionally the most successful boxing nation, arrived in Melbourne with a team described by an American newspaper as “the worst Olympic team ever to leave these shores”. They duly struggled at the lower weights and lost two members who failed to make the weight but found redemption through light-heavyweight " [:a {:href "/athletes/8626"} "Jim Boyd"] " and the destructive performances of heavyweight " [:a {:href "/athletes/8749"} "Pete Rademacher"] "."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The host nation, Australia, claimed a single bronze medal which was their first in boxing in nearly half a century."] "\n\n"] "\n\n" [:h2 {} "Events"] "\n" [:table {:class "table table-striped"} "\n" [:thead {} "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Event"] "\n" [:th {} "Status"] "\n" [:th {} "Date"] "\n" [:th {} "Participants"] "\n" [:th {} "NOCs"] "\n"] "\n"] "\n" [:tbody {} [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/22769"} "Flyweight (≤51 kilograms), Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "23 November –  1 December 1956"] "\n" [:td {} "19"] "\n" [:td {} "19"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/22793"} "Bantamweight (≤54 kilograms), Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "23 November –  1 December 1956"] "\n" [:td {} "18"] "\n" [:td {} "18"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/22816"} "Featherweight (≤57 kilograms), Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "23 November –  1 December 1956"] "\n" [:td {} "18"] "\n" [:td {} "18"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/22839"} "Lightweight (≤60 kilograms), Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "23 November –  1 December 1956"] "\n" [:td {} "18"] "\n" [:td {} "18"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/results/22862"} "Light-Welterweight (≤63.5 kilograms), Men"]] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic"] "\n" [:td {} "24 Nove